  ],
  "Clan Creator": [
   "Clan Creator victory"
  ],
  "BBQ": [
   "Tripe BBQ"
  ],
  "Baby": [
   "A plush of Baby from Super Monkey Ball."
  ],
  "wild": [
   "Their philosophy is that everything has to be \"wild,\" so they make their sandwiches big, bold, and crispy. When it comes to fried chicken, these birds have always been at the top of the pecking order."
  ],
  "OFF": [
   "Change settings for Autosave. \n<color=striking>If OFF is selected, your progress will not be saved automatically. \nPlease be careful.</color>"
  ],
  "Judgment": [
   "<symbol=case_file_head>You've Got A Lot of Mail!\n\n　<symbol=case_file_subhead>Some fun items have been sent to Yagami's office to enhance the Judgment experience.\n　<symbol=case_file_subhead>These can be claimed from the dropbox just outside Yagami's office. Have fun!\n"
  ],
  "Wear Me": [
   "What is the \"Wear Me\" thing?",
   "Not only can you enjoy the thrill of fast-paced, high-level mahjong, you can even play with the exciting Wear Me rule!",
   "(A new mahjong parlor at Nakamichi Alley, huh... What is this \"Wear Me\" rule, though?)",
   "You said you can play using a special rule here? Wear Me, wasn't it?",
   "So how's the Wear Me rule treatin' you?"
  ],
  "Tiger": [
   "My jacket's blue and white, and there's a tiger embroidered on the back. It says \"Tiger\" on it, too."
  ],
  "baggage": [
   "You probably mixed up \"baggage\" and \"cabbage.\" But I think it's also called \"luggage\"?",
   "I suppose it's less confusing in English, since anything you carry around can technically be considered baggage. Even pain."
  ],
  "cabbage": [
   "You probably mixed up \"baggage\" and \"cabbage.\" But I think it's also called \"luggage\"?",
   "I just asked a customer, \"Would you like me to hold your cabbage?\" in English... But they didn't understand at all.",
   "See, I knew cabbage wasn't the right word..."
  ],
  "luggage": [
   "You probably mixed up \"baggage\" and \"cabbage.\" But I think it's also called \"luggage\"?"
  ],
  "take you out": [
   "I think they wanted to \"take you out.\" As in, eliminate you."
  ],
  "take it to go": [
   "It's another way of saying \"take it to go.\""
  ],
  "toilet": [
   "I always thought it was just \"toilet\" in English."
  ],
  "takeout": [
   "'Kay. There was this customer who ordered something for \"takeout.\" What's that supposed to mean?"
  ],
  "Nice to michi": [
   "Hey, Michio-kun. That's not right, remember? You're supposed to say, \"Nice to michi\" when you greet someone!"
  ],
  "softcloud": [
   "Your number is the 555 one, and your email is on softcloud, right?"
  ],
  "RPG": [
   "Hahaha! You're like a hero taking on a stupid fetch quest in an RPG, Yagami-shi. Now make haste, oh brave warrior!"
  ],
  "bangbangbusiness": [
   "First, you go to a deserted area and you post to Chatter with the hashtag, \"bangbangbusiness.\""
  ],
  "bang bang business": [
   "But if you go up to him and say, \"bang bang business,\" he'll sell you a gun."
  ],
  "MaiTube": [
   "Whoa, it's Sana Mihama! The one that's got all that indie music on MaiTube!"
  ],
  "Old King Cole was a merry old so": [
   "I'll be back to marry you faster than you can say, \"Old King Cole was a merry old soul and a merry old soul was he\"!"
  ],
  "ul and a merry old soul was he": [
   "I'll be back to marry you faster than you can say, \"Old King Cole was a merry old soul and a merry old soul was he\"!"
  ],
  "company": [
   "Lonely? You just got paid, man. Why don't you go and buy some \"company\"?",
   "...Why would buying a company help? Besides, I don't think I could run one all by myself."
  ],
  "M Side Cafe": [
   "Apparently the boss is really going for Kiriko-chan, the girl who works at M Side Cafe."
  ],
  "Wette": [
   "We'd better stop before this turns into a Wette and Wild showdown..."
  ],
  "Wild": [
   "We'd better stop before this turns into a Wette and Wild showdown..."
